# EnterprisePulse API

Backend of the EnterprisePulse ERP: a **NestJS 11 modular monolith** on **PostgreSQL 17 + Prisma 6**,
with Redis (cache, BullMQ queues), Socket.IO (realtime notifications), S3-compatible storage (RustFS) and SMTP (Mailpit in dev).
The web client lives in a separate repository (`enterprise-pulse-web`) and consumes this API only through the OpenAPI document.

## Layout

```
src/
  config/           typed env (zod) + AppConfigService
  common/           cross-cutting: request context, guards, decorators, filters, pagination, CASL ability
  infrastructure/   prisma, redis, queue, storage, mail (technical adapters, no business rules)
  modules/<name>/   one folder per business module: controller, service, dto/, events, listeners
prisma/schema/*.prisma   multi-file schema, one file per domain
prisma/migrations/       committed migrations, never edited after merge
```

## Rules that always apply

- Code, identifiers, comments and commit messages are **English**. User-facing strings shown in the UI are translated by the web app; API error messages stay English.
- Every endpoint is under `/api/v1`, documented in Swagger (`/docs`) and protected by default.
  Use `@Public()` only for genuinely anonymous endpoints and `@RequirePermissions('module:action')` for everything else.
- Multi-tenancy: business data is scoped by `companyId` (and optionally `branchId`) taken from `RequestContext` / `CurrentUser`, **never** from the request body.
- Modules talk to each other through exported services or domain events (`EventEmitter2`, e.g. `workflow.approved`), never by importing another module's Prisma models directly into controllers.
- Long or retryable work (mail, exports, integrations) goes to a BullMQ queue, not inside the request.
- Money and quantities use Prisma `Decimal`; never JS floats for persisted amounts.
- Document numbers come from `NumberingService.next(companyId, code, tx)` inside the same transaction that creates the document.
- Approval-backed documents (leave, purchase requests...) start a workflow with `entityId` = document number
  and update themselves in a listener filtered by `definitionCode` (see `hr/leave.listener.ts`). Transitions only move
  from `PENDING`, so replayed events are harmless; workflow events are emitted with `emitAsync` and awaited.
- Calendar dates (`@db.Date`) travel as `"YYYY-MM-DD"` strings via `toDateOnly` / `parseDateOnly`
  (`common/dates/date-only.ts`), never as timestamps.
- Self-service endpoints (e.g. `/asset-assignments/mine`, acknowledging a hand-over form) have no `@RequirePermissions`;
  the service checks ownership and widens access with `hasPermission(user, 'module:read')` from `common/auth/has-permission.ts`.
- Cross-module rules are enforced by the owning module's exported service (e.g. HR termination asks
  `AssetAssignmentsService.countActiveForEmployee`), never by querying another module's tables.
- Stock only changes through `StockMovementsService.post(tx, user, dto)` (exported by `InventoryModule`);
  purchasing, sales and counts call it inside their own transaction. Postings are immutable: they lock variant rows
  (`SELECT … FOR UPDATE`, sorted ids), decrement with a conditional `updateMany` (no row → "Insufficient stock"),
  and append `StockTransaction` ledger rows ordered by `seq`. Corrections are new movements, never edits.
  Call `notifyLowStock` after the transaction commits.
- Sales reservations (`StockReservation`, one per order line) are created on order approval and reduced by deliveries.
  ISSUE / TRANSFER postings may not take a balance below other orders' reservations; a delivery passes
  `{ reservationOrderId }` to `post` so its own reservation does not block it. Available = on hand − reserved.
- Partner balances only change through `PartnerLedgerService.post` / `reverse` inside the document transaction
  (invoices debit / credit, returns credit, cancellations reverse). Lock the partner row before a credit-limit check.
- Cash and bank balances only change through `TreasuryService.post` / `reverse` (`modules/finance`); lock the
  account row first, a cash box may never go below zero. Collections (TAH) and payments (ODM) post to the partner
  ledger and settle open invoices of the same currency (explicit allocations or `allocateFifo`, oldest due first);
  cancelling releases allocations and reverses both ledgers. Cheques / notes move only through `ChequesService`
  transitions, each writing a `ChequeEvent`; money moves on collect / pay, a bounce voids the original collection.
- `modules/reports` is read-only and guarded by the owning module's read permission (`sales:read`,
  `purchasing:read`, `finance:read`). Trade amounts go to the company currency at each document's own rate;
  treasury balances at the latest rate. Ranges are validated with `reportRange` (max two years).
- CRM (`modules/crm`, permission `crm:*`): leads convert once into a customer (new or existing; creating one also
  needs `partners:create`) and optionally an opportunity. Stage rules (default probability, quote → `PROPOSAL`,
  win rate) live in the pure `crm/crm-math.ts`. Sales touches opportunities only through the exported
  `OpportunitiesService` (`attachQuote` on quote create, `markWonByQuote` on conversion) inside its own transaction.
  Opportunities with quotes can't be deleted; closed ones are edited only after `reopen`.
- Expenses (`modules/expenses`, permission `expenses:*`): reading / editing your own reports needs no permission
  (scope = `employee.userId` or `createdById`); `expenses:read` sees all, `expenses:create` files for others,
  `expenses:update` manages categories, `expenses:pay` reimburses. Line amounts come from the pure
  `expenses/expense-math.ts` (receipts at their own rate, per diem / mileage = quantity × category rate). Submit
  starts the `EXPENSE_REPORT` workflow (number as `entityId`); payment posts `EXPENSE_PAYMENT` through
  `TreasuryService` in the company currency, reversal books it back. Receipts are files with entity type
  `ExpenseReceipt`, attached to the report on save.
- Projects (`modules/projects`, permission `projects:*`): members work on tasks and log time without a
  permission; `canManage` = `projects:update`, the project manager or a `LEAD` member; costs are visible to
  managers and `projects:read`. Others get 404. Time entries are priced with the member's hourly cost at save
  time (`projects/project-math.ts`); task numbers and board order are assigned under a project row lock.
  Expenses charge projects only through `ProjectsService.assertChargeable` / `addExpenseCost` (approve adds,
  cancelling an approved report subtracts); projects never import the expenses module.
- Payroll (`modules/payroll`, permission `payroll:*`): all amounts come from `payroll/payroll-math.ts` (30-day
  basis, cumulative income tax, minimum wage exemptions); rates live per company and year in
  `PayrollParameter` (fractions in the DB, percentages in the API). Periods go `DRAFT → APPROVED → PAID`, one
  draft at a time, created in month order under a company row lock; `imported` periods are history without a
  treasury entry. Payment posts one `PAYROLL_PAYMENT` for the net total, reversal books it back. Salary
  records dated in a month with a non-draft period are rejected. Employees see their own payslips without a
  permission once the period is approved; drafts read absences and overtime from `AttendanceService`.
- Recruitment (`modules/recruitment`, permission `recruitment:*`, hiring needs `recruitment:hire`): stage
  rules and funnel math live in `recruitment/recruitment-math.ts`; interviews and offers only move an
  application forward. Interviewers need no permission for `/interviews/mine`, their interview and the CV
  link; only participants submit feedback, and the interview completes when nobody is pending. Board order
  and hiring run under a posting row lock. Hiring needs an accepted offer and creates the employee
  (`EmployeesService.createInTx`) and the first salary record (`SalariesService.createInitial`) in the same
  transaction; the posting closes once all openings are filled.
- Performance (`modules/performance`, permission `performance:*`): scoring lives in
  `performance/performance-math.ts`. Launching a cycle creates one review per active employee hired before
  the period ends (reviewer = active manager); after launch only the name and due dates change. A review
  is visible to the employee, the reviewer and `performance:read` (others get 404, drafts are hidden);
  `toDetail` hides manager ratings from the employee until completed and self ratings from others until
  submitted. `performance:update` holders act as reviewer; `/performance-reviews/mine|team` need no
  permission.
- Training (`modules/training`, permission `training:*`): certificate and compliance math live in
  `training/training-math.ts`. Enrollment checks capacity under a session row lock. Completing a session
  marks unlisted seats `NO_SHOW` and sets `certificateExpiresAt` from the end date plus `validityMonths`.
  `/trainings/mine`, `/training-sessions/open`, `enroll-me` and feedback need no permission.
- Support (`modules/support`, permission `support:*`): SLA math lives in `support/support-math.ts`.
  Anyone opens tickets and follows their own (`/tickets/mine`, `GET /tickets/:id`, comments, close,
  reopen, rating, attachments); other tickets return 404. `support:update` holders are agents (assignable,
  internal notes, status / priority / category changes). Status changes go through `statusChange()`,
  which pauses the resolution clock in `WAITING` and pushes `resolutionDueAt` back on resume. Changes run
  under a ticket row lock; attachments are `files` rows with `entityType = 'Ticket'`.
- Contracts (`modules/contracts`, permission `contracts:*`): date rules live in `contracts/contract-math.ts`
  (`actionDate`, `settle`, `reminderDue`, `annualValue`). `GET /contracts/:id` is open to `contracts:read`
  holders and the owner (others get 404); owners must hold `contracts:read`. Only `DRAFT` / `ACTIVE`
  contracts are editable and dates of an `ACTIVE` one change only via renew / terminate. The daily BullMQ
  job (`contracts.processor.ts`, skipped under `NODE_ENV=test`) calls `runAll()`; `POST /contracts/run`
  runs it for the active company. Each contract is processed under a row lock (`lockContract`);
  events written in one transaction get explicit `createdAt` offsets to keep their order.
- Budgets (`modules/budgets`, permission `budgets:read|update|approve`): actuals are never stored; they
  are collected per request from source documents in `budget-actuals.service.ts` (approved / paid
  expense reports and payrolls, issued purchase and sales invoices minus returns, manual
  `budget_entries`). Pure rules live in `budgets/budget-math.ts` (`itemState`, `alertLevel`, `compare`,
  `categoryResolver`, `departmentScope`). A department budget covers its sub-departments. Item mapping
  rules (`BudgetItemsService.assertMapping`): a category belongs to one active item, one catch-all item
  per categorized source, one item for PAYROLL / SALES. `GET /budgets?year` and `GET /budgets/:id` need
  no permission: users without `budgets:read` see only budgets they own. Plans change only in `DRAFT`.
  The daily BullMQ job (`budgets.processor.ts`, skipped under `NODE_ENV=test`) calls `runAll()`;
  `budget_alerts` keeps one alert per budget, item and level until the budget is reopened.
- Fleet (`modules/fleet`, permission `fleet:read|update`): every odometer value is a row in
  `vehicle_odometer_readings` (MANUAL, FUEL, SERVICE, ASSIGNMENT; fuel and service readings cascade with
  their record) and must fit `odometerRange` for its date; `vehicle.odometer` is the highest reading.
  Changes to a vehicle's assignments, readings and fuel run under `lockVehicle` (row lock); one open
  assignment per vehicle is enforced there, and a handover closes the previous one. Fuel `distance` /
  `consumption` are recomputed for the whole vehicle with `fuelFigures` (full-tank method). Pure rules
  live in `fleet/fleet-math.ts`. `GET /vehicles/:id`, fuel and readings are open to the current driver
  (others without `fleet:read` get 404); `GET /vehicles/my` needs no permission. Vehicles with history
  are retired, not deleted. The daily BullMQ job (`fleet.processor.ts`, skipped under `NODE_ENV=test`)
  reminds once per state via `vehicle_documents.remindedState` and `vehicles.serviceRemindedFor`.
- Accounting (`modules/accounting`, permission `accounting:read|update|approve|close`): the chart is the
  Turkish uniform chart (`accounting-chart.ts`, `ACC` system codes); sub-accounts use dotted codes
  (`120.01`), inherit the parent type and roll up into it. Journal entries are `DRAFT` (manual only,
  editable) or `POSTED` (immutable); corrections are reversal entries (`reversesId`). Document entries come
  from `AccountingPostingService.plan()`: one open (not reversed, not a reversal) entry per
  `source` + `sourceId`; POST / REVERSE / REPOST actions; each document is applied in its own transaction
  under `lockAccounting` (advisory lock). Posting rules are pure functions in `accounting-rules.ts`; line
  normalization, trial balance and statements in `accounting-math.ts`. Amounts are in the company
  currency (`toBase`). `settings.accounting.lockedUntil` blocks posting, reversing and automatic entries on
  or before that date. `JournalLine` is excluded from the audit log. The nightly BullMQ job
  (`accounting.processor.ts`, skipped under `NODE_ENV=test`) calls `runAll()`.
- e-Invoice (`modules/einvoice`, permission `einvoice:read|send|update`): a simulation of the Turkish
  GİB e-Fatura / e-Arşiv flow. `send()` builds UBL-TR 2.1 XML (`einvoice-xml.ts`) from a sales invoice and
  stores a `QUEUED` record; the profile comes from `resolveProfile` (receiver alias → TEMEL / TICARI,
  otherwise EARSIV). `nextOutgoingStep` drives QUEUED → SENT | ERROR → DELIVERED → ACCEPTED (TICARI after
  8 days); transitions lock the row (`FOR UPDATE`) and append an `EInvoiceEvent`. The BullMQ `einvoice`
  queue (`einvoice.processor.ts`, skipped under `NODE_ENV=test`) and `POST /e-invoices/sync` run steps.
  Numbers use the `E_INVOICE` (EPF) / `E_ARCHIVE` (EPA) sequences; `resend` keeps the number when the
  series is unchanged. Incoming invoices are recorded via `PurchaseInvoicesService.create`. Sales invoice
  cancel is guarded by `salesCancelCheck`. `settings.einvoice.autoSend` sends on `sales.invoice.created`.
- Count sessions (stock and asset counts) snapshot the expected state when created, are edited only while `DRAFT`
  (lock the header row with `SELECT … FOR UPDATE`) and apply their effects once on completion.
- Attendance (`hr/attendance.service.ts`): wall-clock times are local to the company time zone (`settings.general.timezone`,
  default `Europe/Istanbul`); a record belongs to the work date of its shift, so a night shift's check-out falls on the
  next day. Day results come from the pure `hr/timesheet.ts` (`evaluateDay`), which is unit-tested; keep rules there.

## Commands

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Dev server | `pnpm start:dev` |
| Type check / lint | `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` |
| Unit / e2e tests | `pnpm test`, `pnpm test:e2e` |
| New migration | `pnpm db:migrate --name <change>` |
| Seed demo data | `pnpm db:seed` |

Infrastructure (Postgres, Redis, RustFS, Mailpit) runs from `docker compose up -d` in the workspace root.

After changing DTOs or controllers, regenerate the client in the web repo with `pnpm api:generate`.
